IBus macOS test client
======================

This directory provides a test purpose client on macOS, which connects
to the ibus-daemon through D-Bus, creates an input context and sends
the characters typed in the standard input to the current engine, and
prints out the engine outputs, e.g. the pre-edit text, candidates and
the committed text.

Run `ibus-macos-client` after the ibus-daemon is started, type some
characters followed by Enter to feed them to the engine, and type
"quit" to exit.  An empty line sends the Return key.

The characters are converted to the ibus key events with the macOS
virtual keycode (kVK_ANSI_*) to Linux evdev keycode table in main.mm,
which can also be reused by a real macOS integration implemented with
Input Method Kit (IMK), which renders the pre-edit text and commits
the text with the IMK APIs.
